TITLE: Relational–Dynamical Structural Realism (RDG) vs. Graph Diffusion Geometry (GDG)

[0] FUNDAMENTAL ONTOLOGY LAYERS (RDG)

TYPE SID: StructuralIdentityDomain
  DESCRIPTION:
    - Primitive layer of distinctions and relations.
    - Encodes entities and their relational structure.
  VARIABLES:
    - V : set of vertices / entities
    - E : set of edges / relations
    - R_SID : relational structure on (V, E)

TYPE PED: PropagationEvolutionDomain
  DESCRIPTION:
    - Dynamical law acting on SID.
    - Encodes how relational states evolve.
  VARIABLES:
    - Q_PED : admissibility / dynamical operator on state space
    - t     : evolution parameter (time or generalized scale)
    - K_PED(t) : propagator generated by Q_PED

TYPE QMODE: ModerationAdmissibilityDomain
  DESCRIPTION:
    - Moderates flux and admissibility between SID and PED.
    - Encodes which relational/dynamical configurations are allowed.
  VARIABLES:
    - Q_mode : general admissibility generator
    - A_Q    : admissibility constraints
    - M_Q    : moderation / regulation of flux

TYPE GAMMA: ClosureGeometryDomain
  DESCRIPTION:
    - Emergent geometric structure from SID/PED/QMODE.
    - Encodes metric, curvature-like invariants, and multi-scale organization.
  VARIABLES:
    - F_Gamma : induced metric / distance structure
    - G_Gamma : induced geometric manifold (not necessarily Euclidean)
    - Inv_G   : geometric invariants (dimensions, curvature-like quantities, contraction rates)


[1] GDG SPECIALIZATION (EUCLIDEAN / PED-SLICE CASE)

ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Symmetric operator Q on l^2(V)
  - Diffusion-like dynamics (classical or fractional)
  - Positive definite kernel
  - Euclidean geometry only

TYPE GDG_Graph:
  VARIABLES:
    - V : finite vertex set
    - E : edge set (relational structure)
    - A : adjacency matrix on V
    - L : graph Laplacian (combinatorial or normalized)

TYPE GDG_Operator:
  VARIABLES:
    - Q := L (or related symmetric operator)
    - Spectrum: {lambda_j} with 0 = lambda_1 < lambda_2 <= ... <= lambda_n
    - Eigenvectors: {psi_j} forming an orthonormal basis of l^2(V)

TYPE GDG_Propagator:
  VARIABLES:
    - alpha : diffusion order (alpha = 1 classical, alpha in (0,1] fractional)
    - t     : diffusion time
    - K_alpha(t) := E_{alpha,1}(-t^alpha * Q)   (Mittag-Leffler or exponential)
      SPECIAL CASE alpha = 1:
        K(t) = exp(-t * Q)

TYPE GDG_Metric:
  VARIABLES:
    - F_alpha,t(v,w) := (e_v - e_w)^T K_alpha(t) (e_v - e_w)
    - X_ij(t) := K_ii(t) + K_jj(t) - 2 K_ij(t)   (GDG squared distance matrix)
  PROPERTIES:
    - F_alpha,t is a squared Euclidean distance matrix
    - Symmetric, conditionally negative, semidefinite
    - Rank <= n - 1
    - Belongs to Schoenberg cone of spherical Euclidean distance matrices

TYPE GDG_Embedding:
  VARIABLES:
    - x_alpha,t : V -> R^{n-1}
    - || x_alpha,t(v) - x_alpha,t(w) ||^2 = F_alpha,t(v,w)
  PROPERTIES:
    - Unique up to orthogonal transformations O in O(n-1)
    - Embedding space R^{n-1} is representational, not ontological

TYPE GDG_GeometricInvariants:
  VARIABLES:
    - Distances: F_alpha,t(v,w)
    - Radius: R(t) of embedding sphere
      Asymptotic behavior: R(t) ~ exp(-t * lambda_2)
    - Angles: induced inner products from embedding
    - Effective dimension: d_eff from spectral scaling
    - Contraction rates: controlled by spectral gap lambda_2
    - Curvature-like behavior: governed by Q^2 in short-time expansion

SHORT-TIME EXPANSION (alpha = 1):
  - K_t = I - t Q + (t^2 / 2) Q^2 + O(t^3)
  - F_t(v,w) = (e_v - e_w)^T K_t (e_v - e_w)
  - Leading local geometric behavior ~ Q^2

SPECTRAL FILTERING:
  - K_t psi_j = exp(-t * lambda_j) psi_j
  - High-frequency modes (large lambda_j) decay rapidly
  - Low-frequency modes (small lambda_j) persist
  - Diffusion acts as spectral filter, generating large-scale geometry


[2] GDG ONTOLOGICAL HIERARCHY

LEVEL 0: Ontology
  - (G, dynamics)
  - G = (V, E) relational structure
  - Dynamics = operator Q acting on l^2(V)

LEVEL 1: Representation
  - Q : l^2(V) -> l^2(V)
  - Hilbert space l^2(V) is representational, not fundamental

LEVEL 2: Emergent Geometry
  - Family of metrics {F_alpha,t}_{t>0}
  - Geometry = invariant relational organization generated by spectral dynamics

LEVEL 3: Embedding
  - x_alpha,t : V -> R^{n-1}
  - Embedding space R^{n-1} is a representational carrier of relational metrics


[3] RDG GENERALIZATION (BEYOND EUCLIDEAN GDG)

RDG SID LAYER:
  VARIABLES:
    - V : entities
    - E : relations
    - R_SID : general relational structure (not restricted to graphs)

RDG PED LAYER:
  VARIABLES:
    - Q_PED : general dynamical / admissibility operator
    - K_PED(t) : propagator (not necessarily diffusion, not necessarily symmetric)
    - Spectrum may be generalized (non-self-adjoint, non-Hermitian, etc.)

RDG QMODE LAYER:
  VARIABLES:
    - Q_mode : general admissibility generator
    - A_Q    : admissibility constraints (which configurations are allowed)
    - M_Q    : moderation of flux and relational transitions

RDG GAMMA LAYER:
  VARIABLES:
    - F_Gamma : induced metric or generalized distance structure
    - G_Gamma : induced relational manifold (possibly non-Euclidean)
    - Inv_G   : geometric invariants (dimensions, curvature-like quantities, contraction regimes, universality classes)

RDG PRINCIPLE:
  - Geometry is the closure (Gamma) of SID/PED/QMODE:
    Gamma(SID, PED, QMODE) -> (F_Gamma, G_Gamma, Inv_G)
  - Geometry is emergent, not primitive.
  - Geometry is the relational form taken by spectral/admissibility dynamics.


[4] STRUCTURAL COMPARISON: GDG vs. RDG

GDG:
  - SID: finite graph (V, E)
  - PED: symmetric diffusion operator Q on l^2(V)
  - QMODE: effectively absent (pure diffusion, no moderation)
  - GAMMA: Euclidean metric F_alpha,t, embedding into R^{n-1}
  - Geometry: Euclidean, positive definite, Hilbert-space representational
  - Invariants: distances, angles, effective dimension, contraction rates, symmetry classes

RDG:
  - SID: general relational domain (not limited to graphs)
  - PED: general dynamical/admissibility operator (not limited to diffusion)
  - QMODE: explicit moderation/admissibility layer
  - GAMMA: general relational geometry (not necessarily Euclidean)
  - Geometry: emergent manifold from closure, possibly non-Euclidean, multi-layered
  - Invariants: all structural invariants surviving SID/PED/QMODE moderation
    (locality structure, curvature-like behavior, contraction regimes,
     universality classes, functional roles, dynamical niches, relational equivalence classes)


[5] GENERAL STRUCTURAL PRINCIPLE (GDG + RDG)

PRINCIPLE:
  - Whenever relational dynamics admit a spectral articulation via an operator Q,
    a geometry can emerge as the relational organization of spectral dynamics.

FORM:
  - Given:
      SID: relational structure
      PED: operator Q on appropriate state space
      QMODE: admissibility/moderation (RDG general case)
    Then:
      Temporal / spectral evolution of Q generates:
        - Kernel-like structures (K(t))
        - Metric-like structures (F(t))
        - Geometric invariants (Inv_G)
      Geometry is:
        - Not primitive
        - Fully determined by relational dynamics
        - Objectively invariant once generated
        - A compressed representation of dynamical information


[6] SUMMARY SENTENCE (ASCII-FRIENDLY)

  GDG:  Geometry = Euclidean shadow of diffusion on graphs.
  RDG:  Geometry = general relational manifold induced by SID/PED/QMODE closure.


